detail:
Trans Hate argues that Trans people are hated. Trans Rights argues that Democrats should stop harassing trans people. Trans rights are human rights. Throwing trans folks under the bus harms everyone. Trans activists bring attention to their issues. Imposing gender apartheid harms trans people. Demonization of trans people is a problem.

@joho.bsky.social: “Jesse Signal, who will screenshot this and name my employer, claims "The public pays attention to trans issues because trans activists wanted them to." That's the wisdom he brings to the conversation.”

Trans Hate (58.8%) says Trans people are hated. Trans Rights (41.2%) says Trans people deserve respect and rights.

Movie Appreciation argues that the movie is ostentatious but lovable. The movie is underrated and deserves a sequel. The movie is enjoyable despite mixed reviews. The movie has a fascinating construction of character. The movie is cheesy but enjoyable. Street Fighter argues that the movie has cool animation and fun fights. It's a fun watch with great references for fans. The movie is campy and has a ridiculous supervillain energy.

@cloutstrife1st.bsky.social: “Going from how bad street fighter was to how unbelievable You can see everything was. It was crazy whiplash. That was the best movie this year. I saw everything bro. I feel so many things right now.”

Movie Appreciation (79.7%) says People appreciate a movie. Street Fighter (20.3%) says Street Fighter movie is fun and entertaining.

Therapy Effectiveness argues that Therapy may not help everyone. Therapy Misused argues that Some people misuse therapy language to claim victimhood. Others refuse therapy and argue with definitions instead.

@cheesecakechik.bsky.social: “But also idk maybe stop abusing therapy language to make yourself the victim because you’re in your tenth midlife crisis this year and you’re depressed about that”

Therapy Effectiveness (83.3%) says Therapy may not help everyone. Therapy Misused (16.7%) says Some misuse therapy language.

Getting Blocked argues that I am instantly blocked. a mutual blocked me. Social Media Blocks argues that People block others on social media.

@ed3d.net: “realized I did had not blocked the guy running the shitheel Gaming For Gamers (Woke) site approximately when he tried to quote-dunk a buddy of mine and his replies filled with misgendering aftermath: the 404 media of games”

Getting Blocked (57.5%) says Users are getting blocked. Social Media Blocks (42.5%) says People block others on social media.

WNBA Finals argues that the WNBA Finals will be taxing yet entertaining. The Finals are a high point for the WNBA. The WNBA is building a prosperous future. Valkyries Win argues that Valkyries are a great team. Valkyries have strong defense. Valkyries deserve their success.

@alongcamepoly4thew.bsky.social: “"I've never seen a basketball team that is more of a TEAM than the Golden State Valkyries" - Noa Dalzell 🏀 #gsv #Valkyries #wnba #wnbafinals”

WNBA Finals (57.9%) says the WNBA Finals are entertaining. Valkyries Win (42.1%) says Valkyries win game one.

Data Centers argues that Data centers waste resources. Data centers will be built everywhere. Data centers control people. Data Collection argues that companies need laws to manage data collection. data harvesting is vital for tech companies. data centers store every moment of our lives. sensitive data is not safe with companies. private data can be handled without online access. companies profit from selling personal data.

@anne-azon.bsky.social: “There's a petition against the data center that Houston said we would not get. Here's the link if you're interested in signing/sharing.”

Data Centers (90%) says Data centers are a waste of resources. Data Collection (10%) says Companies collect personal data.
